Z||000000||ounmongk||01-02-2000||02:15 AM||||I bought an '87 SE about five months ago. The engine had about 80K on it, which I though was fine, but now it leaks oil. I've talked to mechanics but they all say I need an engine overhaul. Is there another alternative?  Also, (if worse comes to worse) will a v-6 engine fit in my 4-cyl compartment, and where can I get one? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||01-02-2000||02:25 AM||||You might need an overhaul, but who knows.  What other symptoms is your motor having?  Surely not just an oil leak?  If that's your only problem, it seems like you're about to be taken to the cleaners by your mechanic.  And, yes.  A V6 will fit into your engine bay just fine.  You need pretty much everything from the firewall back for the change, if I remember correctly (although my memory isn't very reliable <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  There are a number of places to get a 2.8, but your best bet (IMHO) would be to buy a wrecked parts car with a 2.8 even if it has to be rebuilt.  You can probably find one of those for a few hundred bucks.  I'll be getting one in a few months with about 75,000miles on it for $300!  Can't beat deals like that! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||ounmongk||01-02-2000||04:10 AM||||well, aside from all of the oil leaking, there's a good loss of power, and the gas pedal needs to be pressed about halfway down until I start moving. Also, gas mileage has gotten pretty crappy, but I think thats because I street race so many people. on that last note, could my driving condition be causing these symptoms? because I'd hate to get dusted by some pimped honda civic. but if it helps I geuss I could let it go by. on the topic of a v-6 engine, what are some remanufactured/recondition companies that I can talk to about finding a motor? thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||01-02-2000||08:50 AM||||I still think your best bet on a 2.8 conversion would be to find a parts car.  That way you know for sure you're getting all of the needed parts and accessories.  They are definitely around if you look.  Aside from the usual places (like Jaspers), you could try ACE (I forget what it stands for now--just having a brain cramp).  Some else here knows the address.  They do alot of 3.1, 3.4, etc, conversions and sell the 2.8s for between $100US (probably needs rebuilt) and $600US (low miles, just drop it in).  But remember, if you buy a motor, you still need the other parts.  Some of the parts you need are: fuel pump, motor mounts (?), dogbone, ECM, wiring harness, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000004||BigDave||01-02-2000||10:03 AM||||at <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>  they have cheby v8 conversion kits.||||reg||1
