Z||000008||ChadMan||01-02-2000||11:39 AM||||I'm with Monkeyman - I bet there's nothing too serious wrong with your 4-banger.  Where's it leaking oil?  Almost all 2.5L 4-cyl Fieros develop oil leaks at the valve cover gasket, which can be easily replaced by a shade-tree mechanic.  And the driveability and gas-mileage problems are pretty common among neglected Fieros, and are usually caused by vacuum leaks or bad electrical components such as sensors.  Does your "Service Engine Soon" light come on when your Fiero is acting up?||||reg||1
